# Repair invitation controls and note-free fallback
Workstream-ID: lea-36
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/36
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed bounded invitation-control repair
Status: DONE
Milestone: Recognize invitation layouts without weakening send safeguards
Dependencies: lea-31

## Purpose
Repair invitation-control discovery when dialog markup, visible text and
accessible labels differ. Prefer a usable note, including an already-open note
box, and permit an opted-in plain invitation only inside an identified invitation
dialog. Keep technical qualification distinct from live-site acceptance.

## Tasks
- [x] Trace the existing fallback and preserve previous source and tracking.
- [x] Implement scoped controls and bounded waits in a separate fictional lane.
- [x] Cover note preference, safe plain actions, dry-run, limits and confirmation.
- [x] Qualify actual fictional DOM variants and directly affected regressions.
- [x] Update affected user and developer guidance without changing unrelated media.
- [x] Deliver the qualified source without controlling independent applications.
- [x] Verify the issue, Project item, backlink and unchanged predecessor records.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Supported invitation dialogs are not restricted to a div element.
- [x] An already-open usable note box is preferred over a plain invitation.
- [x] Exact visible action text can identify a button with a generic accessible label.
- [x] Generic send actions require positively identified invitation context.
- [x] Missing, disabled, hidden or misleading actions never authorize sending.
- [x] An unavailable note uses a plain action only with the explicit option enabled.
- [x] Dry-run never clicks a final invitation send action or marks delivery.
- [x] A click alone is not recorded as confirmed invitation delivery.
- [x] Weekly limits and arbitrary send failures do not trigger unsafe fallback.
- [x] Existing drafts, invitation-versus-note persistence and prior work are preserved.
- [x] Local verification is not represented as live qualification or publication.
- [x] One issue-backed Project item and durable backlink represent this repair.

## Completion evidence
Delivered the bounded connector/selector repair, focused regressions and eleven
directly affected guides to local source. Semantic/native dialogs, exact visible
labels and bounded control waits are supported. Usable notes take preference;
an opted-in generic final action additionally requires identified invitation
context. Existing drafts are protected, including an already-matching dry-run
draft. A final click or disappearing modal alone does not confirm delivery.

All 97 focused cases pass, including 29 actual browser DOM cases on independently
fictional pages, with no skips. Black, Ruff and mypy pass for the changed Python
scope. Exact delivered imports and 68 original-source connector/service boundary
cases pass. All fourteen payload files match the qualified candidate; all 217
other baseline files outside deliberate tracking edits retain bytes and mtimes.
The existing issue-backed item and backlink are independently verified, with all
35 predecessor issue/Project snapshots, mappings and numbered sources preserved.

The initial qualification had 17 temporary-directory setup errors and no product
assertion failures; creating the missing parent enabled the complete reruns.
The first XML was overwritten by a later rerun; retain that evidence limitation
rather than claiming the original report exists. This local repair does not
establish the exact reported live markup or live LinkedIn acceptance. Existing
icon/glossary/media work, independent applications, installed versions and
published releases are unchanged. No live invitation, commit, push or release.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-11: Complete local source delivery and fictional qualification. Keep
  positive delivery evidence, note-versus-invitation persistence and opt-in
  boundaries explicit; do not equate fixture success with live qualification.
- 2026-11-11: Begin the bounded control repair. Preserve lea-31's historical
  completion, all predecessor records, existing icon/glossary changes and private
  setup. No live invitations, installed-app update, independent restart, commit,
  push or release is included.
